 -content/uploads/2026/04/NuestroWorld-Calendar-size-169.png
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://diverseworks.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/0
 4/NuestroWorld-Calendar-size-169.png
UID:27HSNdDsrDUHoLhTG6Fqn
SUMMARY:Jesus Benavente: NUESTROWORLD
DTSTAMP:20260805T111504Z
DTSTART:20260813T000000Z
DESCRIPTION:Opening Thursday\, August 13\, 2026 | 6 – 8 pm\nDiverseWorks @ 
	5601 B Navigation Blvd\nNUESTROWORLD is a satirical solo installation by B
	rooklyn-based artist Jesus Benavente. Featuring newly commissioned works\,
	 NuestroWorld opens on Thursday\, August 13\, 2026\, transforming 5601 B N
	avigation Blvd\, Houston\, TX 77011 into a fictional visitor center for Nu
	estroWorld\, encouraging guests to explore Houston beyond the gallery wall
	s and experience the city as an amusement park. The installation will be o
	n view through September 13\, 2026\, with a closing party on September 11.
	 Gallery hours are Thursday – Saturday\, 12 – 6 pm. Admission is free. \nT
	hrough satire and spectacle\, NuestroWorld examines how cities construct i
	dentity through tourism\, branding\, memory\, and myth\, inviting audience
	s to reconsider Houston’s past and present. The exhibition draws inspirati
	on from pivotal moments in Houston and Texas history\, including the openi
	ng of the Astrodome and Astroworld in the late 1960s\, Selena’s iconic Hou
	ston Livestock Show & Rodeo performances in the 1990s\, and the folklore s
	urrounding Santa Anna’s capture following the Battle of San Jacinto in 183
	6\, highlighting the city’s recurring cycles of ambition\, folly\, and hea
	rtbreak. The title plays on “Astroworld” and uses Spanglish to create the 
	phrase “The World Is Ours\,” reframing Houston’s cultural mythology throug
	h humor\, nostalgia\, and critical reflection. \nOpening Reception\nThursd
	ay\, August 13\, 6 – 8 pm\nArtist and Curator Talk: 6:45 pm \nClosing Part
	y\nFriday\, September 11\, 2026\, 6 – 8 pm\n7 pm: special performance by C
	TS Trio – Queen of Tejano & Latin Tribute \nARTIST BIO:\nJesus Benavente i
	s a visual artist based in Brooklyn\, New York\, and born in San Antonio\,
	 Texas. Benavente earned an MFA from Rutgers University and attended Skowh
	egan School of Painting and Sculpture. Recent exhibitions and performances
	 include Reception Rome\, Italy\; the Whitney Museum of American Art\, New
	 York\; Queens Museum\; LTD Los Angeles\; Performa 13\, New York\; Acre Pr
	ojects\, Chicago\; Chinati Foundation\, Marfa\; the Neuberger Museum of Ar
	t\, Purchase\, NY\; Shin Museum of Art\, South Korea\; Vox Populi\, Philad
	elphia\; and Socrates Sculpture Park\, New York. \nWebsite: http://jesusbe
	navente.net\nInstagram: @testotesto3 \n \n\nhttps://diverseworks.org/event
	/jesus-benavente-nuestroworld/\n\nFrom DiverseWorks
URL:https://diverseworks.org/event/jesus-benavente-nuestroworld/
LOCATION:DiverseWorks\, @ 5601 B Navigation Blvd & Various Locations\, 5601
	 B Navigation Blvd\, Houston\, TX\, 77011\, United States
