BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:OSe35T_7ozxlhLflSOH9Z
SUMMARY:Current Research in EEPS: Dr. Bridger Ruyle\, NYU Tandon School of 
	Engineering
DTSTAMP:20260805T111504Z
DTSTART:20260827T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS) are anthropogenic co
	mpounds that contain at least one –CF3 or –CF2– group and are known as for
	ever chemicals because they cannot fully mineralize in the environment. Al
	though essential for modern agriculture\, medicine\, refrigeration\, and e
	lectronics\, among other industries\, PFAS contamination poses risks to hu
	man health and contributes to climate change. Most research and public att
	ention focuses on a few PFAS. This narrow focus overlooks the many hundred
	s/thousands of additional PFAS known as precursors that can transform into
	 stable\, terminal products in the environment. This presentation will hig
	hlight recent field work\, experimental results\, data synthesis\, and mod
	eling efforts aimed at improving precursor quantification using organofluo
	rine mass balances and environmental fate\, including the importance of so
	il retention and transformation rates. These studies will be used to discu
	ss the role of precursors on the severity and timescales of PFAS contamina
	tion at major point sources to the environment including firefighting trai
	ning facilities\, wastewater treatment facilities\, and farmlands.\n\nhttp
	s://events.rice.edu/event/436101-current-research-in-eeps-dr-bridger-ruyle
	-nyu\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/event/436101-current-research-in-eeps-dr-bridge
	r-ruyle-nyu
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Keith-Wiess Geological Laboratories
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.rice.edu/li
 ve/image/gid/76/width/80/height/80/crop/1/src_region/0/,0/,600/,337/12130_
 Kavraki-RichardsKortum_1.rev.1781278680.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://events.rice.edu/live/image/gid/76/width/8
 0/height/80/crop/1/src_region/0/,0/,600/,337/12130_Kavraki-RichardsKortum_
 1.rev.1781278680.jpg
UID:6kiWXfYSDOtVTD6-9vcsK
SUMMARY:Triple Crown Celebration
DTSTAMP:20260805T111504Z
DTSTART:20260827T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us in honoring Lydia Kavraki (https://news.rice.edu/news/2
	025/national-academy-sciences-elects-lydia-kavraki-member) and Rebecca Ric
	hards-Kortum (https://news.rice.edu/news/2025/richards-kortum-elected-nati
	onal-academy-medicine)\, two scholars whose careers exemplify the highest 
	ideals of research\, innovation\, mentorship and service.  Through groundb
	reaking discoveries\, commitment to students\, and work that has improved 
	lives around the world\, they have advanced their fields and inspired the 
	next generation of researchers\, engineers and scientists. They are also t
	he only two researchers in Texas elected to all three National Academies\,
	 an extraordinary distinction held by fewer than 35 living researchers nat
	ionwide.  The program will feature reflections from university leadership\
	, perspectives from colleagues\, and a conversation with the honorees on t
	he work\, values and experiences that have shaped their remarkable careers
	.RSVP for this special event! (https://engrice.wufoo.com/forms/the-triple-
	crown-of-discovery/)\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/live/events/432386-triple-
	crown-celebration\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/432386-triple-crown-celebration
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Duncan Hall
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
