UID:b8VQRUsnLRxhKHJEO_UtT
SUMMARY:Engineers in the C-Suite: Leslie M. Duke\, Chair and CEO of Burns &
	 McDonnell
DTSTAMP:20260805T111504Z
DTSTART:20261022T230000Z
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE SPEAKER  &#160\;  A proven leader and collaborator\, 
	Leslie Duke built her career on aligning business strategies with client n
	eeds\, building business in new and existing marketplaces by driving innov
	ation and developing next-generation leaders to advance the firm's vision 
	and values. Safety is at the core of every decision she makes. &#160\;Her 
	top commitment as CEO is to the safety and well-being of employee-owners\,
	 clients\, partners and the communities the firm serves.  Prior to her rol
	e as chair and CEO\, Leslie served as regional president and general manag
	er of the firm's South Central Region. &#160\;Leslie helped expand the fir
	m's regional client base from an initial Houston client to over 650 local\
	, regional and national clients in numerous marketplaces such as power uti
	lity\, petrochemical\, refining\, manufacturing and space exploration. &#1
	60\;Leslie's integral role in launching Burns &amp\; McDonnell's engineer-
	procure-construct (EPC) delivery method led to the development and success
	ful execution of numerous multimillion-dollar projects. &#160\;During her 
	tenure\, Leslie's region delivered over $4 billion in revenue for environm
	ental\, consulting\, engineering\, procurement and construction services. 
	 Leslie joined Burns &amp\; McDonnell in 1999 as a structural engineer and
	 advanced through a series of leadership roles\, including opening offices
	 in Austin\, Dallas and Fort Worth\, Texas and Raleigh\, North Carolina wh
	ere she served as general manager. &#160\;She became a senior vice preside
	nt in 2014 and\, in 2016\, was named the firm's first female president.  L
	eslie earned a bachelor's degree in civil/structural engineering from Texa
	s Tech University and was named a Texas Tech Distinguished Engineer in 201
	8. &#160\;She is an emeritus member of the Dean's Council for the universi
	ty's School of Engineering.  Leslie and her husband\, Travis\, have two ch
	ildren. She is a member of the United Way of Greater Kansas City board\, T
	he Economic Club of Kansas City and the Civic Council of Greater Kansas Ci
	ty. &#160\;She and Travis served as co-chairs of the Ronald McDonald House
	 of Kansas City Spark of Hope Gala. &#160\;&#160\;  __ABOUT THE ENGINEERS 
	IN THE C-SUITE SPEAKER SERIES  Hosted by the Rice Center for Engineering L
	eadership (RCEL) (https://www.rcelconnect.org/)\, Engineers in the C-Suite
	 features executives and thought leaders from technology organizations who
	 uniquely employ or depend on engineers. &#160\;These accomplished leaders
	 share experiences in navigating change and how engineers can equip themse
	lves to lead the way. &#160\;Through this series\, learn about how product
	s and workplaces are being disruptively transformed through technological 
	advancements\, and how engineers are expected to not just adapt to but lea
	d this transformation.  Previous Engineers in the C-Suite speakers include
	:Mark Lashier\, Chairman and CEO\, Phillips 66 (Fall 2025)    (video: http
	s://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9Oql-Yp92lg&amp\;t=19s (https://www.youtube.co
	m/watch?v=9Oql-Yp92lg&amp\;t=19s))  Sandra Johnson\, CEO of SKJ Visioneeri
	ng and former CTO of IBM Africa (Fall 2024)    (video: https://www.youtube
	.com/watch?v=wJlT3xvHhIk) (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wJlT3xvHhIk))An
	tonio Neri\, CEO of Hewlett Packard Enterprise (Spring 2024)    (video: ht
	tps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yBwYQvrfM14&amp\;t=4s) (https://www.youtube.
	com/watch?v=yBwYQvrfM14&amp\;t=4s))Jim Whitehurst\, former CEO of Red Hat 
	and President of IBM (Fall 2023)    (video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?
	v=ty2M4Dw9pcg) (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ty2M4Dw9pcg))  &#160\;REGI
	STRATION  Check back soon for RSVP link!\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/live/e
	vents/429513-engineers-in-the-c-suite-leslie-duke-chair-and-ceo\n\nFrom Ri
	ce University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/429513-engineers-in-the-c-suite-les
	lie-duke-chair-and-ceo
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Duncan Hall
